API-12: make EN_SOURCEMASS the source's current mass inflow rate

Source->Smass is documented as the actual mass flow rate, and
EN_SOURCEMASS returns Smass * 60 as mass/minute. EPANET 2.0 divided the
mass added by the time step; the v2.2 quality rewrite dropped that, so
Smass became the total mass added since the start of the run and
EN_SOURCEMASS returned that total times 60. Store the mass added over
the latest quality step divided by the step length, and 0 when the
source adds nothing, so EN_SOURCEMASS is again a rate in mass/minute.

Requires: WQ-04

Apply from the root of an EPANET checkout at 83e25bb, after
WQ-04_fix.patch:
    git apply API-12_fix.patch

diff --git a/src/quality.c b/src/quality.c
index 918cd70..0fd1c0c 100644
--- a/src/quality.c
+++ b/src/quality.c
@@ -484,6 +484,7 @@ double findsourcequal(Project *pr, int n, double volout, long tstep)
     // Return 0 if node is not a quality source or has no outflow
     source = net->Node[n].S;
     if (source == NULL)    return 0.0;
+    source->Smass = 0.0;
     if (source->C0 == 0.0) return 0.0;
     if (volout / tstep <= Q_STAGNANT) return 0.0;
 
@@ -526,8 +527,8 @@ double findsourcequal(Project *pr, int n, double volout, long tstep)
     // Source mass added over time step = source concen. * outflow volume
     massadded = c * volout;
 
-    // Update source's total mass added
-    source->Smass += massadded;
+    // Update source's mass inflow rate (mass/sec)
+    source->Smass = massadded / tstep;
 
     // Update Wsource
     if (time->Qtime >= time->Rstart)
